------------------------------------------
- How Can We Access ArrayList Elements? -
------------------------------------------

Now that we know how to declare ArrayList variables and to instantiate ArrayList objects, let's look at how we can access the 
elements of an ArrayList.

Consider again, the previous example, declaring an ArrayList variable named names, and instantiating an ArrayList of String 
values.

ArrayList<String> names = new ArrayList<String>();

-----------------------------------------------
	Adding an Element to an ArrayList
-----------------------------------------------

Let's create a new String object and add a reference to this String to our ArrayList.

String myName = "Phill";

names.add(myName);

Notice that we do not use square brackets and indexes to add an element to an ArrayList, as we would with an array. 
The ArrayList class defines a number of methods that allow us to add, insert, and remove elements from an ArrayList.

** Use the add method - To add an Element to an ArrayList **

When we call the add method of an ArrayList, we must pass an argument that evaluates to the value that wil be stored in the 
ArrayList. This value will be stored in a new element that will be appended to the end of the current ArrayList.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
	Retrieving a value stored in an ArrayList
-------------------------------------------------------------------

Similarly, we can retrieve a value stored in an ArrayList using another method named get. The get method takes, as an argument, 
an index value. For example, if we currently have an ArrayList of Strings named names, and this ArrayList contains 3 elements, 
then we can access the first element like this.

names.get(0);

Notice that, just like arrays, the first element of an ArrayList is located at index 0. Likewise, the last element in an 
ArrayList will be located at index size - 1.

** Use the get method - To retrieve an element from ann ArrayList **

-------------------------------------------------------------------
	Additional ArrayList Methods
-------------------------------------------------------------------

ArrayLists have a number of useful methods. The following table lists a few.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|			Method				Description								 |
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
		add(Object to_add)		Add an element to the ArrayList. Object is appended to the end of the ArrayList.
		add(int index, Object to_add)	Insert an element in the ArrayList at the given index
		remove(int index)		Remove the element at an index in the ArrayList
		size()				Returns the number of elements in the ArrayList
		get(int index)			Returns the element at given index in the ArrayList
		set(int index, Object toSet)	Replaces the existing element at given index with the object toSet
		clear()				Removes all the elements from the ArrayList
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A complete description of the ArrayList class can be found in the https://docs.oracle.com/javase/7/docs/api/java/util/ArrayList.html